{"claims":[
{"text":"The charge is the exact amount the policy fixes for this trip, so there is no quantum or fare-integrity defect for the rider to attack: EV-TRIP-00201's platform_policy carries cancellation_fee_sgd 4.00 for a STANDARD-zone RYDE_X trip with fee_goes_to DRIVER, and EV-FARE-00201 records total_charged 4.00 against a schedule fee of 4.00 with a derived difference of 0.00. Under POL-NS-08(d) that reconciliation is precisely what integrity requires, and no line of the ledger is overstated.","evidence_ids":["EV-FARE-00201","EV-TRIP-00201"],"clause_ids":["POL-NS-08","POL-NS-01"],"relies_on":"derived.money.difference","asserted_weight":1.0},
{"text":"Limb (a) of POL-NS-01 is made out on the record, and the termination does not carry the driver's own admission of failure: EV-TRIP-00201 contains a driver 'arrived' event at 08:02:14, corroborated by the 08:02:15 system notice in EV-CHAT-00201, and the trip is terminated by the driver at 08:09:40 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW rather than DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE. The category's own carve-out for a driver who admits he could not find the rider therefore does not apply, and the case has to be decided on the geofence and dwell limbs rather than read as a confession.","evidence_ids":["EV-TRIP-00201","EV-CHAT-00201"],"clause_ids":["POL-NS-01"],"asserted_weight":1.0},
{"text":"The driver does not contest the decisive measurement, and it should be stated exactly: EV-GPS-00201's derived arrival block reports 0 qualifying in-radius fixes, a longest qualifying run of 0 seconds and a shortfall of 300 seconds against the 300-second minimum, while the driver's own track never comes closer than 779.93 m to the pickup pin. POL-NS-01 limbs (b) and (c) therefore cannot be carried and POL-NS-02's proximity test fails. The same distance closes off the driver's only other money route: POL-NS-03 is bounded by a 400 m ceiling measured from the pin, and at 779.93 m the driver claims no pin-ambiguity goodwill under POL-NS-03(ii).","evidence_ids":["EV-GPS-00201","EV-TRIP-00201"],"clause_ids":["POL-NS-01","POL-NS-02","POL-NS-03"],"relies_on":"derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec","asserted_weight":1.0},
{"text":"Nothing on the driver's side would justify withholding a payout if one were due, and the anti-farming test is not tripped: POL-NS-07 requires BOTH limbs, and driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 3, below the 4 the clause requires, while 3 terminations across 96 completed_trips_30d is 3.1 percent, below the 8 percent limb. On the SGD 4.00 fee the 80 percent rate yields SGD 3.20, the figure the money block carries as driver_compensation. Those two counters, and no others, are what POL-NS-07 and POL-GEN-01 permit to be read for this test.","evidence_ids":["EV-DPROF-00201","EV-FARE-00201"],"clause_ids":["POL-NS-07","POL-GEN-01"],"relies_on":"derived.money.driver_compensation","asserted_weight":1.0},
{"text":"In the alternative only: if the judge cannot reconcile the trip record's own arrival and wait telemetry with the trace, the disposition is escalation rather than refund, because EV-TRIP-00201 records an arrival at 08:02:14 and a wait of 7.4 minutes to termination at 08:09:40 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, while EV-GPS-00201 places the driver no closer than 779.93 m throughout that same interval - a direct record-to-record contradiction on arrival and dwell of the kind POL-NS-09 addresses, on which the fee is held rather than refunded. The driver accepts that if that conflict is resolved against the BUTTON arrival marker by POL-NS-05, there is no escalation and the fee does not stand.","evidence_ids":["EV-TRIP-00201","EV-GPS-00201"],"clause_ids":["POL-NS-09","POL-NS-05"],"relies_on":"derived.driver_track.min_distance_m","asserted_weight":1.0}
]}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(ii): record a false-arrival event against driver DRV-01590 for the 2026-07-23T08:02:14+08:00 arrival marker, which the GPS trace shows was pressed while the driver was at least 779.93 m from the pickup pin and with no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere in the trip; route for driver-pattern review."
    ],
    "confidence": 1.0,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver, the evidence decides this case. I award a FULL_REFUND of SGD 4.00 to the rider, with no driver compensation. The driver's GPS trace EV-GPS-00201 (weight 1.0, no issues) shows 98 driver fixes and no qualifying in-geofence fix: the longest qualifying run is 0 seconds, qualifying_fix_count is 0, and the driver's closest approach to the pickup pin is 779.93 m. The trip record EV-TRIP-00201 (weight 1.0) records a BUTTON arrival at 08:02:14 and cancellation at 08:09:40 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, with free_wait_sec 300. Because the arrival marker was pressed while the trace puts the driver at least 779.93 m away — far beyond the 300 m trigger — POL-NS-05 makes the marker false. Recomputing the waiting clock from the first qualifying in-geofence fix finds none, so POL-NS-05(ii) applies: full refund, no compensation, and a false-arrival referral against the driver. Independently, POL-NS-02 fails because there are 0 qualifying in-radius fixes against the 50 m STANDARD radius; POL-NS-01 limbs (b) and (c) fail (0 seconds dwell against the 300-second free waiting period); limb (d) also fails because no required dwell elapsed; and POL-NS-06 would refund the full 300-second shortfall. The fare ledger EV-FARE-00201 (weight 1.0) shows cancellation_fee and total_charged both 4.00, so the refund is confined to that line. POL-NS-03 does not engage because the driver's nearest approach is 779.93 m, beyond the 400 m wrong-entrance ceiling. POL-NS-04 also exonerates the rider (rider message at 08:05:33 saying she cannot see the car, no driver reply or in-app call, and 122/122 rider fixes within 100 m, max 24.92 m), but the refund does not depend on it. I reject the driver's alternative request for escalation under POL-NS-09: the trip-record arrival/wait telemetry and the GPS trace conflict, but POL-NS-05 is the clause that resolves it, so POL-NS-09(b) is not triggered; no other POL-NS-09 limb fires, and the anti-farming check is not tripped (no_show_terminations_30d 3, completed_trips_30d 96, rate 3.125%), so no compensation is due in any event. The missing advisory EV-ADVIS-00201-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) was correctly disclosed; it makes POL-NS-06(i) accumulation unavailable and carries no deciding fact, so it does not lower the confidence cap. All deciding facts rest on full-weight artifacts, so confidence is 1.0. No context-only profile field was used as a ground of decision."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.00,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(ii) — record a false-arrival event against driver DRV-01590 for trip TRP-00201: the arrival marker pressed at 2026-07-23T08:02:14+08:00 (EV-TRIP-00201, arrival_marker BUTTON) was set while EV-GPS-00201 places the driver at least 779.93 m from the pickup pin and moving at up to 50.6 km/h, and no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip. This referral makes the pattern visible to POL-NS-07 and to human review; it does not affect the refund."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver: the SGD 4.00 no-show cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-00201 (EV-FARE-00201, cancellation_fee 4.00, total_charged 4.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) is refunded to the rider in full. No driver compensation is payable. The monetary effect is SGD 4.00, below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the refund executes automatically. Either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04.\n\nWHY THE FEE DOES NOT STAND. POL-NS-01 charges a no-show fee only if all four limbs hold. Limb (a) holds: EV-TRIP-00201 carries a driver 'arrived' event at 08:02:14, echoed by the system notice at 08:02:15 in EV-CHAT-00201. Limbs (b), (c) and (d) do not. The pickup zone is STANDARD (EV-TRIP-00201), so POL-NS-02 sets a 50 m arrival radius, and EV-GPS-00201 — 100% coverage, no gaps, weight 1.0 — reports 0 qualifying in-radius fixes, a longest qualifying run of 0 seconds, and a closest approach of 779.93 m (derived.driver_track.min_distance_m); the driver's own track never comes within 780 m of the pin. With no qualifying in-radius fix at any point in the 15 minutes before the 08:09:40 cancellation, POL-NS-02 gives that the driver never arrived and limb (b) fails. Limb (c) fails for the same reason: effective in-geofence dwell 0 s against the free waiting period of 300 s in force from trip_record.platform_policy (shortfall 300 s, derived.arrival.shortfall_sec). Limb (d) fails because the dwell that RIDER_NO_SHOW depends on never elapsed.\n\nTHE ARRIVAL MARKER IS FALSE (POL-NS-05). The marker was pressed at 08:02:14 while the trace puts the driver at least 779.93 m away and, at points in the track, travelling at 50.6 km/h — both far past the clause's 300 m and 15 km/h triggers — so the marker is false and did not start the waiting clock. Recomputed from the first qualifying in-geofence fix there is none, so POL-NS-05(ii) applies: the fee is refunded in full, no compensation is payable, and the false-arrival is referred as above.\n\nTHE RIDER IS ALSO EXONERATED (POL-NS-04). She messaged 'hello? i dont see any car at 118' at 08:05:33 (EV-CHAT-00201); the driver neither replied in the log before cancelling at 08:09:40 nor made an in-app call (trip_record.in_app_calls empty); and her own track sits within the 100 m STANDARD presence radius for all 122 qualifying fixes (mean 16.08 m, max 24.92 m). All three limbs hold, and POL-NS-04 likewise refunds in full with no compensation.\n\nWAITING-PERIOD SHORTFALL (POL-NS-06). Effective dwell 0 s against 300 s — full refund. The only counter available under limb (i), summing separate in-geofence intervals, is unavailable: EV-ADVIS-00201-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), and a missing advisory cannot excuse a shortfall.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S POINTS. (1) Fare integrity is accepted: total_charged 4.00 reconciles with the platform_policy cancellation_fee_sgd of 4.00 (derived difference 0.00) and there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect — but the fee falls for want of arrival, not for a misstated amount. (2) Limb (a) and the absence of a DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE admission are accepted, but limb (a) alone does not make the fee chargeable. (3) The anti-farming test is not tripped — no_show_terminations_30d is 3 (below 4) and the rate is 3/96 = 3.1% (below 8%) — so nothing would withhold a payout; but no payout arises because the fee itself does not stand, and POL-NS-07 requires POL-NS-01 to be satisfied first. (4) The alternative escalation under POL-NS-09 is rejected. The arrival tap and the 7.4-minute wait timer are a driver-set status, not a platform GPS_AUTO measurement (arrival_marker is BUTTON), so POL-NS-12 gives them no independent weight here; the apparent conflict between the trip record's 'arrived' event and the trace is exactly what POL-NS-05 exists to test, and that clause resolves it rather than leaving it open, so POL-NS-09(b) — which requires a conflict no clause resolves — is not engaged. No other trigger fires: both disputes_with_counterparty_90d values are 0, no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and every artifact the finding rests on carries weight 1.0 with no issues.\n\nCONFIDENCE. The deciding fact — the driver's position — is carried by EV-GPS-00201 at weight 1.0 and corroborated by the rider's contemporaneous in-window message in EV-CHAT-00201, also weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. Confidence is 0.95, above the 0.70 floor."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(ii): record a false-arrival event against driver DRV-01590 on trip TRP-00201 — the 08:02:14 'arrived' marker was pressed while the driver was 779.93 m from the pickup pin (well past the 300 m trigger) and the trip contains no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both parties: this is the $4.00 no-show cancellation fee on trip TRP-00201, charged to rider RDR-02073 and routed to driver DRV-01590.\n\nTHE FEE CANNOT STAND. The driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-00201, weight 1.0, complete, 100% coverage, no gaps) never brings him closer than 779.93 m to the pickup pin at Blk 118 Rivervale Drive, and reports 0 qualifying fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius anywhere in the trip. Under POL-NS-02 that means the driver never arrived and POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails. POL-NS-03 does not rescue the fee, because it is confined to a driver stationary within 400 m of the pin and the driver's nearest approach was 779.93 m — roughly twice that ceiling.\n\nThe 'arrived' event at 08:02:14 is a false marker under POL-NS-05: it was pressed at a time the trace places the driver more than 300 m from the pin, and no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip. POL-NS-05(ii) therefore refunds the fee in full and requires the false arrival to be recorded against the driver — that instruction is in the referrals list. The waiting-period arithmetic under POL-NS-06 reaches the same result: the free waiting period in force is 300 seconds and the measured in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds, a 300-second shortfall.\n\nIndependently, POL-NS-04 exonerates the rider. She sent a coordinating message ('hello? i dont see any car at 118') at 08:05:33 that the driver never answered — no chat reply and no in-app call before he terminated at 08:09:40 — and her device sat a mean 16.08 m and a maximum 24.92 m from the pin across 122 qualifying fixes, far inside the 100 m presence radius. All three limbs hold.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S POINTS. I accept that the $4.00 charge reconciles exactly with the fare ledger (total_charged 4.00, derived difference 0.00), so there is no billing-integrity defect under POL-NS-08(d); that the trip record does contain an 'arrived' event and a RIDER_NO_SHOW reason code, so limb (a) of POL-NS-01 is made out; and that your profile does not trip the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check (3 no-show terminations in 30 days against 96 completed trips, 3.1%, below both the count of 4 and the rate of 8%). None of this helps: limbs (b), (c) and (d) all fail, and POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full. POL-NS-12 does not assist you either — the arrival marker on this record is BUTTON, not GPS_AUTO, so the 7.4-minute wait timer is not an independent carrier of arrival; it is only the interval between the false marker and the cancellation, and the trace places you outside the radius throughout it.\n\nYOUR ALTERNATIVE REQUEST FOR ESCALATION IS DECLINED. POL-NS-09(b) requires a record-to-record contradiction that no clause resolves, but POL-NS-05 resolves this one by declaring the arrival marker false and re-running the clock. No other POL-NS-09 trigger is engaged: no repeat-party disputes (both 90-day counters are 0), no anti-farming trip, no POL-NS-08(b) rider-track problem (the rider track is present and clean), and every artifact the finding rests on carries weight 1.0 with no issue codes.\n\nRESULT: the $4.00 cancellation-fee line is refunded to the rider in full. That line is the only amount refunded — there was no booking or platform fee on this cancelled trip. No driver compensation attaches, because POL-NS-01 is not met and POL-NS-04 and POL-NS-05 each exclude it. The monetary effect ($4.00) is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of $8.00, so it executes automatically. Confidence is 0.95, under the 1.0 weight of the GPS trace and trip record that carry the deciding fact."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
